================================================================================
=  VIMTUTOR ADVANCED  --  Table of Contents                                   =
================================================================================

  Welcome back! You know the basics already: h j k l to move, i a o to
  insert, x dd u to delete and undo, /pattern to search, :w :q to save
  and quit. This tutor picks up where that one left off -- windows,
  buffers, registers, macros, quickfix, folding, mappings, and the
  plugin features your setup installed: completion via coc.nvim, a
  status line, colorschemes, git, and more.

  HOW THIS TUTOR WORKS

  ~ Just like the original tutor, every lesson opens as a SCRATCH COPY.
  ~ Type freely -- your changes are thrown away when you quit with :q!
  ~ (the plugin quietly edits a temporary copy so nothing can break).
  ~ Every lesson ends with the :Tutor number of the next one. Come back
  ~ to this index at any time with:

        :Tutor

  ~ From this index, put the cursor on a |01|-style entry and press
  ~ <Enter> to open that lesson.

  PRACTICE FILES

  Every lesson is copied into a scratch folder together with all other
  lessons and the demo files from lessons/demo/. The file and buffer
  exercises therefore use REAL files you can hop between. Peek now:

        :e 05-<Tab>     (type :e 05- then press Tab, then Enter)
        :ls             (the buffer list -- you are in buffer 1)
        :e 00-<Tab>     (back to this index)

  VERSIONS

  Tested with Vim 9.1+ and Neovim 0.10+. Where the two editors differ,
  the lesson says so. Check which one you are in:

        :echo has('nvim')        (prints 1 in Neovim, 0 in Vim)

  TABLE OF CONTENTS

  |01|  Windows and splits
  |02|  Buffers and tabs -- the mental model
  |03|  Registers beyond basics
  |04|  Macros: recorded power
  |05|  Visual modes and text objects
  |06|  Search, :s, :global, and the quickfix list
  |07|  Marks and jumps
  |08|  Folds
  |09|  Your config file: mappings, plugins, colorschemes
  |10|  Files, :args, sessions, and netrw
  |11|  Terminals and git (fugitive)
  |12|  Completion and LSP with coc.nvim
  |13|  Cheat sheet: the advanced keys on one page

  Shortcuts:  :Tutor 13  for the cheat sheet at any time,  :Tutor 9  to
  re-read how the plugins are configured.

================================================================================
